# client-email-history.auth-guard.must-fail.patch
#
# Targets: AC-18 (whole-module auth guard negative control).
# Authored by: developer seat (agent-seat-separation.companion.md — the seat
# that knows the exact line it changed authors the mutant; the prover applies
# it blind, confirms RED, then reverts — never reading src to construct it).
#
# Revision 2 (repair-loop cycle 3): the first revision mutated ONLY the
# `guard:` member in `client-email-history.services.ts`. The prover confirmed
# it applies/reverts cleanly but never flips AC-18 RED: `refresh()` in BOTH
# `useClientReceivedEmails.actions.ts` and `useClientReceivedEmail.actions.ts`
# carries an INDEPENDENT pre-check —
#   if (!service.isAvailable.value) throw new NotAuthenticatedError();
# — that short-circuits before `query.refetch()` is ever called, so stripping
# only `guard:` is masked: the pre-check throws regardless of whether the
# query layer's `guard` exists. The reverse is equally true and was verified
# the same way: stripping ONLY the two actions-layer pre-checks (leaving
# `guard:` in place) also stays green, because TanStack's `refetch()` still
# runs the disabled query's `queryFn`, where the untouched `guard` rejects
# with `NotAuthenticatedError` before `request()` fires, and `refresh()`'s
# second check (`if (error instanceof NotAuthenticatedError) throw error;`)
# forwards that rejection — the exact same observable outcome. The two
# mechanisms are REDUNDANT gates over the same predicate
# (`service.isAvailable` / `isAddressable(clientId.value)`); AC-18's
# "forced read rejects" assertions only go RED when BOTH are removed in the
# SAME mutation, verified empirically (developer's own run, cycle 3 dispatch)
# before authoring this revision — 5/7 tests stay green, exactly the two
# "forced read" assertions flip RED, matching this file's "Expected RED"
# below.
#
# Revision 3 (repair dispatch, client-email-history rework to product-catalogue
# parity): the services.ts hunks' context lines carried a `withSplitCount:
# true,` line immediately above `guard:` in `loadList` — removed from
# `loadList` by the rework — so both hunks no longer matched. Re-context'd
# against the current file (loadList also gained `placeholderData:
# keepPreviousData` after `staleTime`); the mutated lines themselves —
# the `guard:` member in both `loadList`/`loadOne`, and the actions-file
# pre-checks below — are unchanged from Revision 2.
#
# Mutates (three files, one combined mutant):
#   1. client-email-history.services.ts — removes the `guard:` member from
#      BOTH `loadList` and `loadOne`, leaving only `enabled:` in place.
#   2. useClientReceivedEmails.actions.ts — removes `refresh()`'s
#      `if (!service.isAvailable.value) throw new NotAuthenticatedError();`
#      pre-check.
#   3. useClientReceivedEmail.actions.ts — removes the identical pre-check
#      from its own `refresh()`.
#
# Expected RED: with no authenticated client session, `enabled: () =>
# isAddressable(...)` still stops the query from auto-firing (AC-18's
# "makes no request" assertion, and AC-5/AC-16, stay GREEN), but a FORCED
# read — `actions.refresh()` on either composable — no longer rejects with
# NotAuthenticatedError before or during `query.refetch()`. AC-18's two
# "any forced read is refused as not-authenticated" assertions go RED.
#
# Apply / verify / revert:
#   git apply <this file>     # mutate
#   pnpm test <AC-18 spec>    # must go RED (exactly 2 of 7 tests)
#   git apply -R <this file>  # revert — must return to green
#
